A||N||10||chris6878||Fiero Vs. Dodge Neon||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||01-23-2000||09:15 PM||||Hey everyone...<P>I have a question... who would win...  my friend has a 4 door dodge neon 4cyl auto, and i have a 85 GT fiero, V6 auto...      he was following me one night on a curvy road, (my fiero hates wet curves..)   on each little strecth i would get away a little, but the curves always got me, so i had to slow down.. and he would catch up...    there is a 1/4 mile strecth close by...    i may challenge him this summer when the roads are good and dry....    i know i can get him easly on the curves on a dry road....     he thinks his little neon is bad.....    what would the results be.... ?<P>my other 85 Gt gets a V8 this summer... maybe i should just wait till then...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||01-23-2000||10:12 PM||||Have you checked out this topic about Neons yet?<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/000012.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/000012.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||01-23-2000||11:13 PM||||I can give you some first hand knowledge here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>My mother's work car is a 4cyl, 4 door, auto Plymouth neon.  This car has absolutely NO torque until you rev the crap out of it.  You should be able to take him off the line no problem.  It goes pretty good once it gets up there, but the shifts, even at full throttle, are very slow.  I think I estimated a 0-60 time of about 16 seconds.... (it's that slow...)  Challenge this guy.  You should whip the crap out of him.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||01-23-2000||11:31 PM||||If you cant take it any where curves or not you must be doing something wrong||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||01-24-2000||10:23 PM||||Time for new tires, cuz the curves are where the fiero will do the most damage. I actually got pretty humiliated by a neon one night at a stoplight to stoplight. Stupid me tried to match his 7000 rpm shift points. We all know what happens then. I stay pretty careful in drag races with 5 speed dohc neons. Automatics, I do't know.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||01-25-2000||09:29 AM||||Neons are great autocrossing cars.  I don't know if Dodge intended that but they are very capable at SCCA events and there are a lot of them that show up.  In stock trim, they will probably kick Fiero but.  <P>But what would you rather be seen driving?  Nobody ever got laid driving a Neon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>There are some fugly (****ing ugly) '60s Chevys that will eat Porsches and Ferraris at the stop light.  <P>But what would you rather be seen driving?<P>I didn't buy the Fiero so I could be the baddest boy on the block.  I think it holds it's own.<P>By the way, is the Neon even in the Fiero's SCCA class?  Automotive dedign does not stand still and that Neon has a 12 year and growing advantage.  <P>If the Neon owner still thinks his car is hot shit, tell him to challenge you in an 84-88 Dodge, his choice of model too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||Greg Piet||01-25-2000||01:43 PM||||Well I had a 2.5l 4 cyl plymouth sundance.  It handled well but wasnt even close to my V6 fiero's acceleration.  The sundance handles really well, but i raced a friend in his 86ish dodge charger shelby with a 2.2 turbo.  I still schooled him in my plymouth but it was a good romp.<BR>I rented a few Neons over the past few years(all of them had under 10k miles so they were still "new", and they were slower and handled worse than my plymouth.  With the comparison between the plymouth/neon, the plymouth was a better car, and in the plymouth/fiero comparison, the fiero wins, so I dont imagine a neon schooling a fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-25-2000||05:17 PM||||Tom88gt--Exactly what year was the last time you actually sat in your Fiero?!  I've gotten horizontal in some pretty small cars ('75 VW Superbeetle), but I'm fairly sure you'd have to be some kind of gymnast to get laid in a Fiero.  Best of luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW--You said the "S" word and Cliffs program didn't edit it out.  You might want to do that yourself.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||01-25-2000||07:25 PM||||I leased a 4 door 5-spd Neon for three years in between Fieros and it was a DOG! I was shocked when I saw the replys to this topic and wonder what the hell was wrong with the one I had! It literally SUCKED!||||reg||5
Z||000010||Eddie.H||01-25-2000||07:34 PM||||Iam with gokart that nasty looking thing cant be that fast.even if it is it still will never look as fast as the FIERO!!!||||reg||6
Z||000011||Dan86gt3.8||01-25-2000||09:38 PM||||weell about a month ago i was out at a local cruise strip.  that night there was a r/t neeon 9the one with stripes, and he thought he was a real bad a$$.  Well first of all this guy was an idiot!  and he kept on doing the patented rice boy fly-by.  he would never  slow down and race fair, and when I was at a light talking to a friend he pulled up on the othe side of me and told me to "take your $hit home, dawg"  needless to say this guy was the typical ricer idiot and I would rather be in a fiero over a neon (particularly a riced outneon)any day!  Anyways i welcome a challenge from anyone but this particular neon owner was a true a$$ in every sinse.  I also know what you mean about the fiero getting loose on wet roads its typical for me too!||||reg||6
